HOPPY redesign and MuJoCo simulation
=====================================

This repository builds on the HOPPY educational kit developed by the
RoboDesignLab at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign:

  J. Ramos, Y. Ding, Y. Sim, K. Murphy, D. Block.
  "HOPPY: An open-source kit for education with dynamic legged robots."
  arXiv:2010.14580
  https://github.com/RoboDesignLab/HOPPY-Project

Scope of the MIT license in this repository
--------------------------------------------
The LICENSE file applies to the original work of the authors listed in
CITATION.cff:

  - the MuJoCo simulation, controller and analysis scripts under mujoco/
  - the mechanical redesign and printable parts under CAD/ (the IMP-* parts
    and the bird-type four-bar leg)
  - the firmware changes for continuous hopping under Microcontroller/
  - the documentation (README files and figures)

Redistributed upstream material
--------------------------------
Some material here comes from the upstream HOPPY kit and is included for
reproducibility and to credit its authors. The upstream repository does not
publish an explicit license file, so this material remains under the terms of
its original authors and is not relicensed by the MIT file above:

  - Simulator_MATLAB/        the original MATLAB reference simulator
  - HOPPY_Technical_Guideline.pdf and the upstream BOM
  - the original firmware example that Microcontroller/ is based on
  - any original CAD provided by the kit

If you reuse this project, please credit both the upstream HOPPY kit and this
redesign. See CITATION.cff.
